en:
The girls' restroom on the east side of the first floor.
That's the one.
Inside that restroom there's a grimy, blackish stain.{p}

With an aura, you usually get a kind of premonition as you get close.
Like, oh, there's one around here.
The stronger the aura, the stronger you feel it.{p}

That's what I did, too.
I just couldn't leave a girl who looked about to cry, after all.
To be safe, we decided to go in and see the stain for ourselves.{p}

The door opened, and Ms. Hida came in.
She was holding a towel.
Something was wrapped up in it.{p}

Apparently, when one of her gang went to visit Saijo in the hospital, her whole face was covered in a horrible stain.
They say that stain looked exactly like the one in the restroom.
No treatment could get rid of the stain on Saijo's face, and after that she didn't want to see anyone, and then she vanished without a trace.{p}

Ms. Hida smiled at us, relieved, maybe.
"I see. Thank you, everyone.
...To tell you the truth, the girl who was made to lick that restroom stain was me."{p}

When I asked the other girls, they said her name was Tomita, and that she was always bragging about having a sixth sense.
But no matter how long we waited, Tomita didn't come out.
We got nervous and peeked inside the restroom.{p}

Tomita went limp and passed out.
...In other words, pathetically enough, I got saved by a girl.
The teachers noticed the commotion, came running, and took Tomita away.{p}

And yet, far from getting angry, Hosoda was grinning.
"If anything happens?
And what exactly do you think is going to happen?"{p}

......Something was wrong.
Alarm bells started ringing in my head.
And just then...{p}

I thought he was going to head for that restroom, but instead he slammed the door shut right in the girl's face.
"H-Hosoda★"
I couldn't believe what he'd done, and I cried out without thinking.{p}

His thick hands reached for my neck.
And still, my body wouldn't move at all.
Just as I'd made up my mind that if I died, I'd at least come back and haunt him for sure......{p}

Suddenly, he froze dead still.
I couldn't believe it.
Black hair was wrapped around his arms.{p}

But the hair was so strong it dragged me along with him.
Just as the fear crossed my mind that I'd be pulled into the wall too...
A cold hand came down on my shoulder.{p}

The instant I did, Mr. Ashimura's body rose into the air.
And in the blink of an eye, he was dragged into the wall of the stall.
The wall should have been solid, but it looked like jelly.{p}

"AAAAAAAAAAAAGH!"
With a scream from Mr. Wakatsuki that seemed to shake time and space itself, the weight of him leaning on my body vanished.
Finally able to move again, I quickly turned around to look.{p}

All that was around me were the girls who'd come with me, huddled together and crying.
I had no idea what had happened, so I asked the girls.
But they just kept crying, and I couldn't get anything out of them.{p}

A few days later, the girls finally came back to school, and I was able to find out from them what had happened.
Their stories didn't make much sense at all.
Each of them told it differently, but putting it all together, it seems it went something like this.{p}

They say another face appeared inside the mouth of the face in the stain.
A stain with a face that looked like it was begging for help...
I haven't gone into that girls' restroom since, so I don't know if it's true.{p}

"If you insist, I can't stop you.
But if anything happens, run away at once."
With that, he walked off toward the faculty room to get ready.{p}

"It was when I was thirty-two.
The year I was first assigned to this school.
In the class I was put in charge of then, there was a girl named Kaori Nitta.{p}

"What was in that medicine... was actually Kaori's blood.
Who knows where she learned it, but Kaori had found out that mixing a young woman's blood with special herbs makes a medicine that preserves youth.
Kaori didn't want me to grow old, so she was mixing the medicine with her own blood.{p}

One day, Kaori appeared at my bedside.
Kaori said she couldn't bear to watch me growing old.
Then she said, 'I'll do something about it for you,' and vanished.{p}

that rumors began going around about a stain like a face appearing in that restroom.
And more and more students started getting anemic in there.
I'm sure Kaori was drawing blood from the students who came near the stain."{p}

...In the end, we left the teacher there and went home.
The next morning, I woke up early, of course.
I was worried about Yoneyama.{p}

A stain that had soaked right into the material of the wall wasn't going to come off that easily, was it?
But Saijo told her to get rid of it.
The harder it is, the more fun it is for the bully, right?{p}

The girl kept scrubbing at the stain, crying.
But of course it wasn't going to come off.
Saijo grabbed the girl by the hair and shoved her face against the stain.{p}

"It hasn't come off one bit, has it?
Quit slacking!
You're not going home till it's gone!"{p}

Next to the stain that had offered her the deal the day before, there was another one.
A new face-shaped stain had appeared.
And that face......{p}

With a swish, the knife grazed my arm.
It felt less like pain and more like heat.
I threw myself at the door.{p}
